From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:58:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 86/91] fix(polecat): scope the live-owner guard to real pool
 claims and restore the owner's session id (gcp-mjjg)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three self-review findings on the guard that landed in the previous commit.

Only a `claimed` hook reason can be a duplicate pour. `existing_assignment` and
`ready_assignment` mean the bead already carried this session's identity before
the hook ran, and the release that creates this hazard CLEARS the assignee — so
a released bead can never reach us by those tiers. The guard now runs only on a
fresh pool claim (or an unknown reason, which still checks). That is not just
cheaper, it is a tighter statement of when the hazard exists: a molecule's own
preassigned steps come back as `ready_assignment` at every step boundary, and
paying three `gc` round-trips there was pure startup tax on the hot path.

The restore now always writes `gc.session_id` rather than writing it only when
the owner's id could be read. The hook stamps OUR session id onto the step
during the claim, so omitting the key on an unreadable owner left our binding
standing on a bead we had just handed back — a wrong binding, which is worse
than an absent one. Writing the empty value clears it instead, and the owner's
next write restores the real one. This also drops an unquoted `${var:+...}`
whose word-splitting was load-bearing.

Third, the exemption bookkeeping the new test needs: its fake `gc` dispatches on
the wrapper's argv tail, so its case labels and the assertion on the recorded
tail read as bare `bd` invocations to the no-bare-bd guard. Registered in that
guard's argv-tail allowlist the same way the merge-approval and find-work pack
tests are, with the assertion hoisted into a marked variable so the exempted
line is the data and not the grep.

Validation: the claim-reason gate verified RED (narrowing the condition to
reason == "claimed" alone makes the unknown-reason case skip the guard) then
GREEN. Nine guard cases pass, plus the full gastown shell suite, `go mod
download`, `go vet ./...`, `golangci-lint run ./...`, `validate_registry.py`,
`go build ./...`, `go test ./...`, and the Python pack suite (850 passed, 9483
subtests).
